Germany and Britain developing operational jet fighters by war''s end, and no jet bombers saw combat service.",\n      "relevance": 0.85\n    }\n  ],\n  "fact_count": 7,\n  "coverage_notes": "Research indicates that no British first-generation jet-powered medium bomber was actually used in the South West Pacific theatre during World War II. Jet technology was too immature during the war period, and British forces in that theatre relied on conventional piston-engined aircraft. The question appears to contain a false premise, as jet bombers did not become operational until after the war ended."\n}\n```','\n',char(10)),655,657,0,'markdown_wrap','["markdown_wrap"]','[{"category": "markdown_wrap", "loc": "", "type": "json_invalid", "msg": "Invalid JSON: expected value at line 1 column 1"}]','claude-haiku-4-5-20251001');
