sively piston-engined aircraft, as jet-powered bombers had not yet been developed or deployed operationally.",\n      "relevance": 0.9\n    }\n  ],\n  "fact_count": 7,\n  "coverage_notes": "Research indicates that no British first-generation jet-powered medium bomber was actually used in the South West Pacific theatre during World War II. Jet technology was still developing during the war, and operational jet aircraft were limited to fighters in the European theatre. The question appears to contain a false premise, as all medium bombers in the South West Pacific were piston-engined aircraft."\n}\n```','\n',char(10)),655,646,0,'markdown_wrap','["markdown_wrap"]','[{"category": "markdown_wrap", "loc": "", "type": "json_invalid", "msg": "Invalid JSON: expected value at line 1 column 1"}]','claude-haiku-4-5-20251001');
